<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vendel</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vendel is a parish in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uppland">Uppland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, where rich boat graves excavated from 1881 held helmets, weapons and animal sacrifices. The finds gave their name to the Vendel period of Swedish history, about 550 to 790, just before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a>. Its decorated helmets resemble those of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutton-hoo">Sutton Hoo</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vendel.jpg" alt="Vendel" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User IN433 on sv.wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ottarshogen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
